//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// The loop bound of a stridable region carries a marker, and only the loop that
// was proved disjoint carries it.
//
// A GPU wants each thread to walk a STRIDE through the iteration space, so
// neighbouring threads touch neighbouring addresses. Offsetting the start and
// widening the step is enough for that, which is why `vx.parallel_init` and
// `vx.parallel_step` were all the device clone ever needed.
//
// A CPU worker wants the opposite -- a CONTIGUOUS range, or every cache line is
// fetched by every worker and written back under false sharing. A contiguous
// range means moving the upper bound as well as the lower, so the host clone
// needs the bound marked too. That is `vx.parallel_bound`.
//
// The marker has to be SELECTIVE, and that is the half worth pinning. Only the
// outermost loop was proved to have disjoint iterations. An inner loop walks
// one row of the work the outer iteration owns, and partitioning it across
// workers would hand each worker a fraction of every row -- numbers that come
// out plausible and wrong. So the checks assert both directions: the outer
// loop's bound store carries the attribute, and the inner loop's bound store is
// a bare `memref.store` with no attribute dictionary at all.
//
// The two loops are given different trip counts (4 outside, 8 inside) so the
// constant in each check names which loop it is talking about. With equal trips
// the checks would still pass if the tag landed on the wrong one.
//
// Flat path only: the tags are emitted in `hir/flatten.rs` and rendered in
// `codegen/flat/emit/memory.rs`, and the legacy AST path has never had them.
//
// REQUIRES: flat-codegen
// RUN: vxc %s --emit-mlir -X mlir=--pass-pipeline="builtin.module(convert-vx-to-standard)" 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

// The host kernel, which is the clone the worker split rewrites.
// CHECK: vx.kernel @vx_npu_kernel_0

// The outer loop: start and bound both marked, and the latch increment with
// them. All three are the assertion -- a bound marked on a loop whose start was
// not would move one end of a range and not the other.
// CHECK: memref.store %c0_i32, %{{.*}}[] {vx.parallel_init}
// CHECK: memref.store %c4_i32, %{{.*}}[] {vx.parallel_bound}

// The inner loop: neither store marked. Written as the bare store rather than
// as a CHECK-NOT so the check fails when a tag appears, instead of passing
// because a pattern happened not to match.
// CHECK: memref.store %c0_i32, %{{.*}}[] : memref<i32>
// CHECK: memref.store %c8_i32, %{{.*}}[] : memref<i32>

// The latch, still marked, after both loops have been set up.
// CHECK: arith.addi %{{.*}}, %c1_i32 {vx.parallel_step}

fn probe() -> f32 {
  let mut o = Tensor<f32, [4, 8]>::uninit();
  spawn on(Topology::GPU) {
    for i in 0..4 {
      for j in 0..8 {
        o[i][j] = i as f32;
      }
    }
  }
  return o[0][0];
}

fn main() -> i32 {
  print(probe());
  return 0;
}
